 "notes": "Moved the Ryobi ONE+ 18V powered range off Pruning saw (belongs with powered cutting tools, pole saw/chainsaw). Old Niwaki GR 210 became a version of the Niwaki GR 210 archetype; GR 270 and Moku stay in m. Old Gardena StarCut Pro L is a StarCut version (old data). Left out: Okatsune loppers (no such product found on retrieved pages), Wolf-Garten loppers and Fiskars pole pruner archetype (no page retrieved; UPX86 kept in m), Felco 221 kept as old model only (Felco page retrieved covers 211), Corona founding year given as '1920s' as on its own page; Niwaki founding 2006 is when Hobson started the business per Gardens Illustrated (sources disagree). Silky Gomboy year 1985 from Silky history page; no other introduction years confirmed. Parallel search was out of credit; Firecrawl rate-limited, so WebFetch used."
